Add a kolla-ansible deployer image.

Kolla-Ansible is installed onto the deploy host with pip and fetches
its collections from Galaxy and git, so two deploy hosts installed a
day apart can run different code against one cloud. Add a kolla-ansible
image which packages the tool, as Kolla packages every service.

Collections are installed at build time into the only path Ansible
searches, so nothing is fetched at run time and ~/.ansible cannot
shadow them. Labels cannot hold build output, so the versions and
source commits are recorded in /etc/kolla-ansible/deployer.json.

